    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0089" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg77"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.83/12–1646: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Egypt</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Tuck</hi>)<anchor n="14" xml:id="d42-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-12-16">December 16,
                        1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2016. Inquiries received by Dept re press accounts attributing to Makram
                        Ebeid<anchor n="15" xml:id="d42-f2"/> statement that US Govt had sent note
                    to Sidki advising him to reach agreement with British. In reply Dept spokesman
                    said Dec 16 that last May we had in fact expressed to both <pb facs="0090"
                        n="78" xml:id="pg78"/> Egyptian and Brit Govts our hope that treaty
                    negotiations might terminate in such manner as to give satisfactory guarantees
                    to Egypt of full sovereignty without at same time running risk of undermining
                    security of Middle East. Spokesman added we still hope satisfactory settlement
                    can be reached along these lines.</p>
                <p>Sent Cairo rptd London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d42-f1" n="14" type="source" xml:id="d42-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. Tuck became Ambassador in Egypt on September 19, 1946.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d42-f2" n="15" xml:id="d42-f2-content">
                <p>Formerly a member of the Egyptian delegation negotiating with the British for
                    revision of the Anglo-Egyptian treaty of 1936.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
